Inspired by Electron's posts, and their .dll implementation method.
The name trainer is kind of null now. Now exe's or anything to run.

## Notes 
The catalog is one `dinput8.dll` placed beside `game.exe`. It forwards the
game's DirectInput calls to the Windows system DLL, then loads a catalog inside
AnyMaker. There is no companion executable or `_internal` folder.

Local creations are read from the current Windows user's
`%APPDATA%\Anymaker\creations`. Workshop creations are found through Steam's
installed library locations. The mod writes startup and failure events to
`%LOCALAPPDATA%\AnyMakerCatalogDll\catalog.log`.

## Features

- Browse and search items and components, including optional color and skin tiles.
- Spawn S01, S02, and S03 keycards.
- Browse local and subscribed Workshop creations; click a tile to place it.
- Adjust creation spawn distance. 
- Hold Delete to target creation, then click to remove the target.

## How To Use
Browse Items or Components, or search directly. Click an image to add the item. Hover for its description.
To remove it, close the game and delete this dinput8.dll from the game folder.

## Setup

1. Copy dinput8.dll next to game.exe in your AnyMaker installation folder.
2. Start the game, load a world, and open your inventory. The catalog appears beside it.

Unofficial mod; not endorsed by the game developer.


